## 3. Things that must be true for it to work
- `ProcessBuild.tsx` imports `openContactOverlay` from `./ContactOverlay`. If ContactOverlay.tsx is somewhere else, fix only that import path.
- The section pins (position: sticky) while you scroll. **No ancestor of it may have `overflow: hidden`, `overflow: auto` or `overflow-x: hidden`**, or the pinning silently breaks. If the rounded panel around the Work section uses `overflow: hidden` for its rounded corners, change it to `overflow: clip`, which keeps the corners and lets sticky work. Check the wrappers in App.tsx too.
- Don't wrap ProcessBuild in anything with a fixed height or `transform`.
- The navbar is fixed on top; that's fine. The section is meant to sit under it.

## 4. Fonts
The component uses `var(--lns-display)` and `var(--lns-body)`, the same variables as the other components. Don't hard-code fonts. Keep "LNS Numerals" first in the display stack so the big percentage counter renders in the rounded number font.
The hand-written "go on, press it" note uses Google Font **Caveat**, loaded by the `@import` on the first line of the component's CSS string. Keep that line first in the string, or the import is ignored.

## 5. Dark mode
The section is drawn in the paper/ink/red palette, like the other paper panels. If the site's dark mode changes the panel colours, add a dark-mode rule that sets `--pb-paper`, `--pb-ink`, `--pb-muted` and `--pb-line` on `.lns-pb` to the dark theme's values. Keep `--pb-red` as it is.

## Check before finishing
- Scrolling into the section pins it. Guide lines draw outward from the centre, the radius ring opens around the red point, and the 12 grid columns grow down one after another.
- In "A layout." each wireframe box draws itself from its left edge to its right edge; the image box widens last and its X draws in.
- In "A typeface." the headline words blur into focus one at a time, then the brand, menu, body copy and button labels type out letter by letter.
- In "A colour." the red dot in the button grows into the arrow circle and the moon artwork wipes down over the X.
- In "A line of code." the code window types out as you scroll, then turns see-through and fades.
- In "Your turn." the finished site breaks apart, the frame shrinks to a card around "Let's talk", the button glides to the centre, the aim lines draw and "go on, press it" writes itself.
- Scrolling up un-types and un-draws everything in exact reverse. Wheel scrolling still looks smooth.
- "Build progress" counts 000% to 100%; "Skip the build" jumps to the end; the final button opens the contact overlay.
- On a 390px phone nothing scrolls sideways and the final button is big enough to tap.
- With "reduce motion" on, the section doesn't pin: it shows the finished site and all 8 steps as a list.
- No console errors.
